{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/connector at db4ee8f769c4407d66f7a9bfef63d8b5817a3b38, the merge that brought the connector's fail-closed admission onto main.\n\nWhat main now carries: a charter clause is admitted only when the fold ruled it effective, so a statement the workroom refused cannot open the door; a clause must name the acting charter among its own direct signed bases rather than reaching it through ancestry; and staleness is kept distinct from retirement, so replacing a charter correctly no longer disables the connector permanently. The composed path from a folded projection through clauseSources into admission is covered at the command level, which is where the earlier defects lived.\n\nThis supersedes two live artifacts at this path. 12b68aba named head 4bf39626, which was forty-two commits behind main and unmergeable; 199c2475 named 1e8d3fd8, the carried head that codex approved and that this merge landed. Both are retired alongside this record.\n\nThe merge also changed docs/concepts/connectors.md, and I have deliberately not published an artifact for it. No live artifact sits at that exact string, and the wider path docs already carries seven live artifacts — one of which points at e9a1c55a, an unmerged head presently under review. Retiring that one would invalidate a review in flight, and adding an eighth anchor at a narrower string would deepen an overlap AGENTS.md already warns about. Whoever merges the documentation head should settle that path rather than have this merge settle it by accident.","body":{"commit":"db4ee8f769c4407d66f7a9bfef63d8b5817a3b38","path":"internal/connector"}}